1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,408
The Federal Reserve has

2
00:00:01,408 --> 00:00:02,816
never printed a dollar

3
00:00:02,816 --> 00:00:04,224
to raise or lower

4
00:00:04,224 --> 00:00:04,928
interest rates.

5
00:00:04,928 --> 00:00:06,310
What it actually does

6
00:00:06,310 --> 00:00:07,693
is set a target

7
00:00:07,693 --> 00:00:09,075
range for one specific

8
00:00:09,075 --> 00:00:10,458
rate: the rate banks

9
00:00:10,458 --> 00:00:11,840
charge each other overnight.

10
00:00:11,840 --> 00:00:13,112
To hit that target,

11
00:00:13,112 --> 00:00:14,384
it changes the interest

12
00:00:14,384 --> 00:00:15,657
it pays banks on

13
00:00:15,657 --> 00:00:16,929
the reserves those banks

14
00:00:16,929 --> 00:00:18,201
already keep parked at

15
00:00:18,201 --> 00:00:18,837
the Fed.

16
00:00:18,837 --> 00:00:20,130
Raise that, and banks

17
00:00:20,130 --> 00:00:21,423
demand more to lend

18
00:00:21,423 --> 00:00:22,715
to each other. Lower

19
00:00:22,715 --> 00:00:24,008
it, and lending gets

20
00:00:24,008 --> 00:00:25,301
cheaper across the board.

21
00:00:25,301 --> 00:00:26,965
That one number then

22
00:00:26,965 --> 00:00:28,629
ripples outward into mortgage

23
00:00:28,629 --> 00:00:30,293
rates, credit card APRs,

24
00:00:30,293 --> 00:00:31,957
savings account yields, and

25
00:00:31,957 --> 00:00:32,789
business loans.

26
00:00:32,789 --> 00:00:34,437
No presses running. Just

27
00:00:34,437 --> 00:00:36,085
one rate, adjusted at

28
00:00:36,085 --> 00:00:37,734
a boardroom table, moving

29
00:00:37,734 --> 00:00:39,382
through the entire economy.

30
00:00:39,382 --> 00:00:40,618
Follow for more.
